leto para todas las plataformas\"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# build-darwin-arm64 (Apple Silicon Mac)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nbuild-darwin-arm64:\n\t@mkdir -p $(DIST_DIR)\n\tGOOS=darwin GOARCH=arm64 go build -trimpath $(LDFLAGS) \\n\t\t-o $(BIN_DARWIN_ARM64) \\n\t\t./cmd/spec-kitti-telemetry/\n\t@echo \"✓ Darwin ARM64: $(BIN_DARWIN_ARM64)\"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# build-darwin-amd64 (Intel Mac)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nbuild-darwin-amd64:\n\t@mkdir -p $(DIST_DIR)\n\tGOOS=darwin GOARCH=amd64 go build -trimpath $(LDFLAGS) \\n\t\t-o $(BIN_DARWIN_AMD64) \\n\t\t./cmd/spec-kitti-telemetry/\n\t@echo \"✓ Darwin AMD64: $(BIN_DARWIN_AMD64)\"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# build-windows-amd64 (Windows x64)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nbuild-windows-amd64:\n\t@mkdir -p $(DIST_DIR)\n\tGOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build -trimpath $(LDFLAGS) \\n\t\t-o $(BIN_WINDOWS_AMD64) \\n\t\t./cmd/spec-kitti-telemetry/\n\t@echo \"✓ Windows AMD64: $(BIN_WINDOWS_AMD64)\"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# clean — elimina binarios compilados\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclean:\n\trm -rf $(DIST_DIR)\n\t@echo \"✓ Directorio dist eliminado\"\n","path":"/Users/luciano.perez/itti/pr-coe-genai-spec-kitti/telemetry/Makefile"}Ahora verifico que el Makefile sea válido con `make -n` (dry-run) y luego un build real. Primero, chequeo la sintaxis del Makefile:


